WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:23.366
- My name is Samad.

00:00:23.366 --> 00:00:25.266
I run C3 Laundry Services.

00:00:25.266 --> 00:00:28.266
We're a cleaning service in Ghana, Accra.

00:00:28.266 --> 00:00:29.400
I have been doing this for

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:30.700
close to nine years now.

00:00:30.700 --> 00:00:31.800
Today, I'll be showing you

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:33.233
how to clean a Persian rug.

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:36.700
This rug has never been cleaned before.

00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:39.133
The rug is located in their dining area.

00:00:39.133 --> 00:00:40.900
It had multiple stains on it,

00:00:40.900 --> 00:00:44.633
food stains, coffee
spillage, drinks, soda,

00:00:44.633 --> 00:00:45.933
everything you could mention.

00:00:45.933 --> 00:00:49.000
It has about 20 years
of dirt sitting in it.

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:50.233
So, first of all,

00:00:50.233 --> 00:00:52.066
you give it a good rinse in the beginning.

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:54.133
The water is always cold.

00:00:54.133 --> 00:00:55.166
If you use hot water,

00:00:55.166 --> 00:00:57.400
it may shrink the fabric
or destroy the fabric.

00:00:57.400 --> 00:01:00.200
You only use hot water in some cases

00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:02.766
where you're treating a particular stain.

00:01:04.566 --> 00:01:06.433
There's shampoo in the watering can.

00:01:06.433 --> 00:01:09.133
You can't use just any
soap for cleaning rugs.

00:01:09.133 --> 00:01:11.800
It's a mixture of shampoo,
the stain removers,

00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:13.200
and then water.

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:14.900
So usually when you apply the shampoo,

00:01:14.900 --> 00:01:15.900
you allow it to sit

00:01:15.900 --> 00:01:17.433
for about five to ten minutes.

00:01:17.433 --> 00:01:19.133
Then you know it's gone really deep

00:01:19.133 --> 00:01:20.233
into the fibers.

00:01:22.966 --> 00:01:25.466
The Persian rug is usually made of,

00:01:25.466 --> 00:01:26.833
I believe it's silk.

00:01:26.833 --> 00:01:29.366
So this rug, I'm not
sure of the exact cost,

00:01:29.366 --> 00:01:32.700
but it should cost between $800 to $1,000.

00:01:37.066 --> 00:01:38.433
So, after putting the shampoo,

00:01:38.433 --> 00:01:40.566
then you scrub with a scrubber,

00:01:40.566 --> 00:01:43.133
or a buffer, some people call it a buffer

00:01:43.133 --> 00:01:45.033
but I call it a scrubber.

00:01:45.033 --> 00:01:49.000
So the buffer basically agitates the dirt,

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:52.600
and it helps get all
the dirt out of the rug.

00:01:52.600 --> 00:01:54.866
So I scrub all around the rug,

00:01:54.866 --> 00:01:57.166
scrub, scrub, give it a good old scrub,

00:01:57.166 --> 00:01:59.566
to get most of the dirt out.

00:02:06.366 --> 00:02:07.200
There's a brush.

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:08.900
So, there are two types of brush,

00:02:08.900 --> 00:02:11.100
the hard brush and then the soft brush.

00:02:11.100 --> 00:02:13.033
So, the type of rug will determine

00:02:13.033 --> 00:02:14.100
which brush you use.

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:16.066
For this one, we use the hard brush.

00:02:16.066 --> 00:02:18.100
Some rugs are handmade.

00:02:18.100 --> 00:02:19.600
You can't use the hard brush.

00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:21.833
You're going to destroy
the fabric of the rug,

00:02:21.833 --> 00:02:24.300
but with this type, it
can handle the hard brush.

00:02:25.900 --> 00:02:27.066
It's not handmade.

00:02:27.066 --> 00:02:30.966
Some parts are handmade,
like the fringe parts.

00:02:35.266 --> 00:02:36.633
You have to scrape the water off

00:02:36.633 --> 00:02:38.533
to get the first scrubbing session

00:02:38.533 --> 00:02:40.166
of the dirt out.

00:02:40.166 --> 00:02:43.533
So, I use a squeegee, or
should I say a scraper,

00:02:43.533 --> 00:02:45.366
a shovel scraper I got someone

00:02:45.366 --> 00:02:46.900
to make for me over here.

00:02:51.733 --> 00:02:54.533
If you pay attention
to my type of scraper,

00:02:54.533 --> 00:02:57.200
you see how it gathers most of the dirt

00:02:57.200 --> 00:02:59.700
and pushes all the water away.

00:03:02.900 --> 00:03:04.300
So, the pressure washer

00:03:04.300 --> 00:03:06.400
helps loosen more dirt in the rug.

00:03:07.900 --> 00:03:09.300
Pressure-washing the rug alone

00:03:09.300 --> 00:03:11.133
cannot get all the dirt out.

00:03:11.133 --> 00:03:14.100
You need the shampoo to help do its magic.

00:03:14.100 --> 00:03:16.666
It's not a one-procedure thing.

00:03:19.366 --> 00:03:21.766
So I give it a good old
rinse with a squeegee.

00:03:23.133 --> 00:03:24.533
Then we flip it to the back.

00:03:25.800 --> 00:03:27.533
It's important to clean the work area,

00:03:27.533 --> 00:03:30.700
so that dirt doesn't
come back into the rug.

00:03:30.700 --> 00:03:33.633
Then you can continue with working.

00:03:36.666 --> 00:03:38.133
The back side will also require

00:03:38.133 --> 00:03:39.600
putting shampoo on it.

00:03:43.366 --> 00:03:44.466
It's the same procedure,

00:03:44.466 --> 00:03:46.433
just that procedure doesn't take as long

00:03:46.433 --> 00:03:47.533
as the top side,

00:03:47.533 --> 00:03:49.900
because usually the dirt is trapped

00:03:49.900 --> 00:03:52.233
more on the top side than the back side.

00:03:58.500 --> 00:04:00.266
When you clean the back, some of the dirt

00:04:00.266 --> 00:04:02.400
somehow goes back to the top part,

00:04:02.400 --> 00:04:04.133
so you have to flip it up

00:04:04.133 --> 00:04:06.233
and redo the whole process again.

00:04:29.533 --> 00:04:31.133
Scrub, scrub, scrub.

00:04:31.133 --> 00:04:33.500
Eventually you realize
the water becomes clear,

00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:34.566
so once it gets clear,

00:04:34.566 --> 00:04:37.166
you know your rug is clean now.

00:04:37.166 --> 00:04:40.433
Persian rugs are not too
delicate, if I may say.

00:04:40.433 --> 00:04:42.400
There are different types of Persian rugs.

00:04:42.400 --> 00:04:44.800
Some require very close
attention to cleaning,

00:04:44.800 --> 00:04:47.966
but some will require the
normal cleaning procedure.

00:04:47.966 --> 00:04:50.400
This one needed extra care,

00:04:50.400 --> 00:04:53.033
because of the fringes especially.

00:04:53.033 --> 00:04:54.033
If you're not careful,

00:04:54.033 --> 00:04:56.200
the fringes are just going to come out.

00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:03.833
So you manually have to apply the shampoo

00:05:03.833 --> 00:05:05.400
with the chemicals onto the fringes,

00:05:05.400 --> 00:05:07.400
then you manually scrub.

00:05:08.700 --> 00:05:11.433
I can use any brush to clean the fringes,

00:05:11.433 --> 00:05:12.933
any hard brush.

00:05:12.933 --> 00:05:14.200
It has to be a hard brush,

00:05:14.200 --> 00:05:16.533
cause you're dealing with years of dirt.

00:05:16.533 --> 00:05:17.500
You need a hard brush

00:05:17.500 --> 00:05:19.600
to be able to scrub all that dirt out.

00:05:30.866 --> 00:05:32.200
Then I use the power washer

00:05:32.200 --> 00:05:34.400
to blow the dirt out of it.

00:05:41.366 --> 00:05:43.100
So, I am using the wet vacuum

00:05:43.100 --> 00:05:46.533
to vacuum most of the
water out of the rug.

00:05:46.533 --> 00:05:49.233
I repeat the process like twice,

00:05:49.233 --> 00:05:51.800
I am able to get at
least 80-90% of the water

00:05:51.800 --> 00:05:54.700
out of the rug before
I leave it out to dry.

00:05:54.700 --> 00:05:57.966
I see some people use
the centrifuge machine,

00:05:57.966 --> 00:06:00.366
where it spins all the water out.

00:06:00.366 --> 00:06:01.800
I believe those who use that machine

00:06:01.800 --> 00:06:04.100
don't have very good weather over there.

00:06:04.100 --> 00:06:06.000
In my country, the sun is always out,

00:06:06.000 --> 00:06:08.500
so it helps dry the rugs quickly.

00:06:09.700 --> 00:06:11.100
It came out great.

00:06:11.100 --> 00:06:12.800
The client was very satisfied.

00:06:12.800 --> 00:06:15.600
The original colors were restored as well.

00:06:15.600 --> 00:06:17.433
I had no idea how the original colors

00:06:17.433 --> 00:06:18.933
looked like. You're unable to tell

00:06:18.933 --> 00:06:20.300
how it originally looks like

00:06:20.300 --> 00:06:21.633
until you're done cleaning.

00:06:22.733 --> 00:06:25.333
It's usually dirt sitting
in there for years

00:06:25.333 --> 00:06:26.766
that makes it heavily soiled.

00:06:26.766 --> 00:06:28.866
It's best to have a
vacuum in your household,

00:06:28.866 --> 00:06:30.200
where once in a while,

00:06:30.200 --> 00:06:32.200
you vacuum all the dirt out of your rug.

00:06:35.600 --> 00:06:39.100
A rug like this can be
cleaned every half a year.

